rea\":\"Control citation accuracy\",\"issue\":\"new_epoch/two_aborts_then_identical_restart: decoding the packed rows gives acceptances at cycles 6, 10 and 14, the forward at 15, the slave ACK at 16, and the master ACK (pre) at cycle 17, not 18. The CYC drop is at cycle 18. Other cycle citations should be mechanically re-derived rather than hand-written.\"},{\"id\":\"F7\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"Resource limits / executability\",\"issue\":\"Canceled-pool members persist for the whole reset epoch and cannot be released without C1. Identical members branch without a quotient. Long single-epoch batches therefore reach MAX_CANCELED_POOL or MAX_HYP and suspend all association judgments for the rest of the epoch. This is sound because it degrades to unresolved, but the effective checked scope may be near zero. The checker must report the suspended-row fraction as a coverage metric, and scoped_pass must not be emitted for any clause that was suspended.\"},{\"id\":\"F8\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"area\":\"K5 scoped_pass labeling\",\"issue\":\"fault/live_order_swap and new_aba/younger_equal_first are reported as scoped_pass. For new_aba/younger_equal_first, the surviving branch has the first forward bound to A2, and that binding is consistent. However, both verdicts must list K5 (forward and side-effect order) as explicitly excluded, so that 'pass' is not read as order preservation.\"},{\"id\":\"F9\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"area\":\"Quantifier semantics\",\"issue\":\"The existential-membership versus universal-safety distinction is correctly stated. The bounded F3 determinization is acknowledged. No proof evidence is claimed. Persisting canceled identities until reset is sound given the absence of C1.\"}],\"required_changes\":[\"Add an unknown tag for an ERR delivered while that master holds an unaccepted stalled request (possible starvation). Do not treat it as K6 invention. Revise the post-exhaustion response-count invariant to allow it.\",\"Make aggregate precedence time-bounded: a DUT violation that precedes the first env violation remains dut_violation.\",\"Reclassify K13 as inferred, document the OPT_DBLBUFFER latency assumption, and cite it as inferred in dependent verdicts.\",\"Restrict K2 None checks and K10 stall-hold comparisons to the identity projection (WE, address, SEL, enabled write lanes).\",\"Replace the F2 and F3 false controls with reachable DUT or stimulus mutations that have covers. Drop the trivially failing strict-< control.\",\"Re-derive all control cycle citations mechanically, including correcting cycle 18 to cycle 17 in new_epoch/two_aborts_then_identical_restart.\",\"Report a limit-exhaustion and suspended-scope metric. Forbid scoped_pass on any suspended clause.\",\"Mark K5 as excluded in every scoped_pass verdict whose outcome depends on unjudged forward order.\"],\"ready_for_implementation\":false}\n```","ttft_ms":66520,"type":"result","duration_ms":83981,"uuid":"94652b27-ca53-43fa-bbd3-b779cebcd13b","ttft_stream_ms":1315,"time_to_request_ms":221,"first_content_frame_ms":1316,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":7917,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":66089,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.488801,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":6074,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
